 "answer": "**Possibly a little better on Sunday, October 18, but don’t count on clear air.** Singapore’s NEA says showers and changing, weakening winds may reduce smoke drifting from Kalimantan, though haze from Sumatra could still reach Singapore. The latest PSI forecast I found is **150–230 (Unhealthy to Very Unhealthy) for Saturday, October 17**—I couldn’t find an official PSI forecast yet for Sunday. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026))\n\nCheck NEA’s next update before planning outdoor activities; conditions can vary through the day.",
